Zend extensions in a program without dlopen

PHP compiles the mechanism that Zend extensions register with only where
it can load one from a file, which needs dlopen. OPcache is a Zend
extension, and built into the program it registers itself with that
mechanism when the program starts; without it, the registration does
nothing, OPcache never starts, and the program's shutdown frees what its
start never made. Radix has no dlopen, as the program is static, so this
keeps the mechanism and makes the loading of a file fail; dl() and the
extension lines of php.ini are not built, as before.

diff --git a/Zend/zend_portability.h b/Zend/zend_portability.h
index 6546ebfb..aae98ba7 100644
--- a/Zend/zend_portability.h
+++ b/Zend/zend_portability.h
@@ -196,8 +196,14 @@
 # define DL_HANDLE					HMODULE
 # define ZEND_EXTENSIONS_SUPPORT	1
 #else
+/* No dlopen(), no loading of a Zend extension from a file: one that is built
+ * into the program, as OPcache is, still has the mechanism it registers with. */
 # define DL_HANDLE					void *
-# define ZEND_EXTENSIONS_SUPPORT	0
+# define DL_LOAD(libname)			NULL
+# define DL_UNLOAD(handle)			((void) (handle))
+# define DL_FETCH_SYMBOL(handle, symbol)	NULL
+# define DL_ERROR()					"Loading a shared library is not supported"
+# define ZEND_EXTENSIONS_SUPPORT	1
 #endif
 
 #if defined(HAVE_ALLOCA_H) && !defined(_ALLOCA_H)
